      "Language": "pol",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "There is evidence that a link exists between the upper and lower respiratory tracts. During the last fifty years many clinical observations has lead to a new pathogenic view of rhinosinusitis and asthma defined as Sinobronchial Syndrome. The inflammatory process in the nose and bronchi explains some of the complex interactions among different clinical diseases, such as rhinosinusitis, asthma, bronchial hyperresponsiveness and viral infections."},
